fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1579684Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1588912Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1692418Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1702294Z ^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1702886Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1703645Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1704019Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1704352Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1705642Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1706141Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1706460Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1707096Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1707407Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1708169Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1709102Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1709855Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1710434Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1710878Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1711073Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1711358Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1711568Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1711959Z    can use Nix.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1712094Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1712198Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1712375Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1712672Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1713144Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1715302Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1715664Z I will:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1717295Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1717755Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1718254Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1718695Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1719119Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1719387Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1719803Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1720487Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1721468Z    /root
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1730380Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1731494Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1742304Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1742950Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1743430Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1744514Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1745141Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1763351Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1763907Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1774776Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1775642Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1776074Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1776394Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.1776670Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
